<title>SENEGAL: Senegal's groundnut oil production fell in 1996.</title>
<headline>Senegal's groundnut oil production fell in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal's groundnut oil production for 1996 (May-Dec season) fell to 588,181 tonnes from 790,617 in the previous campaign, final official figures showed.</p>
<p>Analysts said the decline was due mainly to low production yields.</p>
<p>To boost production in 1997, the authorities have decided to provide farmers with 52,000 tonnes of groundnut seed and 20,000 tonnes of fertiliser and pesticides.</p>
<p>Senegal is expected to produce 950,000 tonnes of groundnut oil in 1977, an advisor at the Ministry of Agriculture said.</p>
</text>
